    "named_events": [],
    "standardized_narrative": "Syndicate 1919 experienced a gross prior year reserve strengthening of $60.2 million in 2021, representing 7.59% of its opening gross claims outstanding. This movement was mixed, with deteriorations primarily in the Casualty division (specifically General Liability and Financial Lines classes for 2017 & prior underwriting years) due to case loss reserve strengthening and late deteriorating large losses. Adverse development was also noted to a smaller extent in Accident & Health, Political Risk, and Aviation. These strengthenings were partially offset by favorable claims development in Technical Risks and Marine divisions for 2018 and prior years, attributed to lower than expected loss experience, benign loss activity (partly due to reduced global flight activity from COVID-19), and lower levels of economic activity.",
